# Root cause: read-only oasis_events query against production Supabase
# (never opened a live ORB session — absolute governance rule) for the
# reporting user's session window, topic T007, 2026-08-26 08:45-08:46 UTC.
supabase execute_sql --project inmkhvwdcuyhnxkgfvsb "
  SELECT type, status, message, payload, created_at
  FROM oasis_events
  WHERE payload->>'user_id' = 'c5a4daf9-190a-4a9e-9638-d6b32f85244a'
    AND created_at BETWEEN '2026-08-26 08:44:00' AND '2026-08-26 08:47:00'
  ORDER BY created_at;"
#   -> session 1 won the guided-topic candidate correctly, taught T007 for
#      44.5 real seconds (497 audio_out_chunks, 13455 tokens), then
#      'orb.session.continuity.persisted reason:"connection"' at
#      08:46:12.799 (confirms _announceDisconnect fired -- a genuine
#      unexpected disconnect, not a clean close).
#   -> session 2 (the reconnect) started with NO guided_topic_narration
#      candidate in its wake-brief list at all
#      (suppress_reason:"all_sources_skipped"), explaining the "new day
#      greeting instead of reading the session" symptom.

# Read orb-widget.js: _announceDisconnect() calls _playAlert(...)
# unconditionally (no _audioEverHeardThisOpen gate, unlike VTID-03727's
